Well, the YASD part was quite S indeed, of the "one more hit" kind. I 
should have been less lazy, go back to refill my stock of full healing 
(and, incidentally, make peace with my god) and learnt to use ranged 
attacks. It was on Asmodeus, or some other demon's lair below Juiblex.

What I really want to talk about is the two main patches used in this game.

First of all is the Pet ranged attack patch (port of D. Shaligram's 
patch for Nethack). I already used it a bit since mages start with 
breathing pet and so I already knew that it was nice. And indeed, 
herding around 10 adult dragons in open spaces turns into some quite 
refreshing breathing madness...

Most important is the full Lethe patch for Slash'em. I also used it for 
quite a time but never managed to reach Medusa with it before. And I 
strongly recommend anybody to use it. It makes things much harder and 
interesting. The super-amnesia power of the Lethe water, especially 
combined with the infamous spell of create pool make levitation/flying a 
must have below Medusa. Thus going for quite a change in the usual AK. I 
did not manage to play well enough with levitation (shopuld have #poly 
into something flying, actually) nor with putting BoH in oilskin sack 
and lost many, many valuable scrolls, potions, memories or weapon/armor 
enchantement (and since it's the ones you bring in Hell, they're indeed 
valuable). I made at least three baths in the Lethe (one via vortex 
expelling me at the wrong place, one with golden naga creating pool and 
one due to a teleport problem).

Overall, the whole passage between Medusa and the Valley of Deads was 
far harder and interesting than any traversal of Hell I've made before 
(well, there is 2 in nethack plus 1.5 in Slash'em). And the Gehennom 
part itself... Well, I never though I could consider usual maze level 
being a nice pause in the game.


It was also the second time I deliberatly get teleportitis (yummy little 
nymph) and the first I manage to Tengu-dance for teleport control.


Oh, and now I'm suffering from PAS (Post Ascension Syndrom) [Yeah, even 
if I didn't ascend, but you know what it is after a good game you don't 
want to start again...] and I'm probably goign to try and adapt a good 
lot of Nethack patch for Slash'em... If things go well, they're should 
be some new patchs soon :-)

